{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"55080","self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/55080","key":"SV-8945","renderedFields":{"statuscategorychangedate":"Today 11:38 AM","issuetype":null,"timespent":null,"project":null,"customfield_10351":"","fixVersions":null,"aggregatetimespent":null,"statusCategory":null,"resolution":null,"resolutiondate":null,"workratio":null,"watches":null,"issuerestriction":null,"lastViewed":null,"created":"Today 11:38 AM","customfield_10021":null,"customfield_10385":null,"priority":null,"labels":null,"customfield_10016":null,"customfield_10019":null,"timeestimate":null,"aggregatetimeoriginalestimate":null,"versions":null,"customfield_10418":null,"customfield_10419":null,"issuelinks":null,"assignee":null,"updated":"Today 11:38 AM","status":null,"components":null,"timeoriginalestimate":null,"description":"<p><b>1. What happens now</b></p>\n\n<p>Clicking a column heading on Technician Utilization sends a fresh request to the server and waits for new rows. The written description asks for the rows already on screen to be reordered without any reload.</p>\n\n<p><b>2. What should happen instead</b></p>\n\n<p>Technician Utilization specification, version 6, requirement S2-R13: \"All six columns... are sortable by clicking the column header... Sorting is applied on screen to the loaded rows (no reload).\"</p>\n\n<p><b>3. How to see it</b></p>\n\n<p>Open Reports &gt; Technician Utilization and set the date range to This Year so there are plenty of rows.</p>\n\n<p>Click the Total Hours heading once, then again.</p>\n\n<p>Watch the table: it briefly clears and refills each time rather than simply reordering.</p>\n\n<p>Exact test data this was seen with: organisation Staging Foothills Group Inc; signed-in user Admin ShopView; active location Staging Heavy Duty - 9919; the other accessible location Staging Lethbridge - 4310; date range This Year (1 January 2026 to 6 August 2026), which returns 29 technicians.</p>\n\n<p><b>4. What was actually shown</b></p>\n\n<p>Each click sent a new request to the report's own data address carrying the sort as part of the request - first with the sort marked not-descending, then with it marked descending. The rows came back from the server rather than being reordered in the page.</p>\n\n<p><b>5. What was ruled out</b></p>\n\n<p>It is not the sort being wrong. The order itself is correct: the first click on Technician sorts Z to A, the next A to Z, with no third state, and Est. Lost Labor sorts correctly both ways.</p>\n\n<p>It is not a one-off. It happened on every column tried - Technician, Total Hours and Est. Lost Labor.</p>\n\n<p>It is not the report reloading for another reason. The date range and the location selection were untouched between the clicks.</p>\n\n<p><b>6. How often</b></p>\n\n<p>Every time, on every column.</p>\n\n<p><b>7. Where it was seen</b></p>\n\n<p>Reports &gt; Technician Utilization, on the QA branch, build v3.5-16cf83f, on 6 August 2026.</p>","customfield_10015":null,"timetracking":{},"security":null,"aggregatetimeestimate":null,"attachment":[],"summary":null,"creator":null,"subtasks":null,"customfield_10285":"","reporter":null,"customfield_10044":null,"aggregateprogress":null,"customfield_10046":null,"customfield_10047":null,"environment":"","customfield_10318":null,"duedate":null,"customfield_10518":null,"progress":null,"votes":null,"comment":{"comments":[],"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/55080/comment","maxResults":0,"total":0,"startAt":0},"worklog":{"startAt":0,"maxResults":20,"total":0,"worklogs":[]}},"fields":{"statuscategorychangedate":"2026-08-06T01:38:47.414-0500","issuetype":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issuetype/10007","id":"10007","description":"Subtasks track small pieces of work that are part of a larger task. (Migrated on 31 Dec 2023 09:01 UTC)","iconUrl":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/vi